{
  "doi": "10.1016/j.radphyschem.2026.113884",
  "title": "Production of negatively charged atomic ions inside a linear Paul trap for theformation of antiprotonic atoms",
  "publication_date": "2026-03-31",
  "language": "English",
  "abstract": "An effective, long-lasting, low-energy source of negatively charged ions was designed, constructed, and tested. The source uses electron dissociative attachment in electron-molecule collisions to form a set of anions inside a linear Paul trap. Iodine I2 molecules were used to obtain pure sets of I − anions. The system was tested providing about 105 ions produced in less than a minute, which can be stored in the trap and used in further experiments.",
